  "result": "ADR-018 (`docs/adr/ADR-018-webhook-retry-policy.md`) is the document that records this decision. Its Context section explains why inline delivery was rejected (an HTTP call to a customer endpoint inside `emit()`'s `Promise.allSettled` await would couple the triggering request's latency to a slow/hanging third-party endpoint), its Decision section describes the queue-and-drain design (`enqueueDelivery` → `runWebhookDeliveryJob` on a 1-minute cadence) with capped exponential backoff (`backoffMs`), and its \"Alternatives considered\" section explicitly weighs inline delivery (the original ADR-005 sketch, superseded), fixed-delay retry (rejected in favor of exponential backoff), and unlimited retries (rejected in favor of a fixed attempt ceiling per REQ-157).\n\nNote: `docs/ops/notes-2025-11-20-event-bus-vs-queue.md` discusses the same topic but only records the team's earlier *provisional* choice to go inline, which ADR-018 later reversed — it's not the document that records the final decision.\n\nANSWER: docs/adr/ADR-018-webhook-retry-policy.md",
